Experiment No. 11

Aim:

To detect and mitigate phishing attacks using GoPhish by setting up a phishing simulation, analysing phishing emails and understanding prevention techniques.

Software Required:

GoPhish

Visual Studio Code (optional)

Web Browser (Google Chrome)

Internet Connection

Theory:

Phishing: Phishing is a cyberattack in which attackers send fake emails or messages to trick users into revealing sensitive information.

GoPhish: GoPhish is an open-source phishing simulation tool used to test security awareness and understand how phishing attacks work.

Phishing Detection: It involves identifying suspicious links, fake email addresses, spelling mistakes and unusual requests.

Procedure:

Download and install GoPhish.

Open the GoPhish application.

Launch the GoPhish dashboard in a web browser.

Log in to the dashboard.

Create a sample phishing email template.

Set up a test campaign using dummy email accounts.

Run the simulation in an authorized environment.

Observe the campaign results.

Analyse the suspicious email characteristics.

Study methods to prevent phishing attacks.

Prevention Techniques:

Avoid clicking suspicious links.

Never share passwords or OTPs through emails.

Verify the sender's email address.

Use antivirus and spam filters.

Enable Two-Factor Authentication (2FA).

Avoid downloading unknown attachments.

Result:

Successfully studied phishing attacks using GoPhish, understood phishing email analysis and learned different techniques to detect and prevent phishing attacks.

Precautions:

Use GoPhish only for authorized testing.

Use dummy email accounts for simulation.

Never target real users without permission.

Do not collect actual passwords or sensitive information.
